      h1 { font-size: 1.6rem; line-height: 1.25; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
      h2 { font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.3; margin: 1.8rem 0 .4rem; }
      p { margin: 0 0 .75rem; }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>

    <p>This page covers the website wowforever.be and the iOS app that goes with it.</p>

    <h2>The app does not ask who you are</h2>
    <p>
      There is no account, no login and no profile. The app never asks for a name, an
      email address or a phone number, and it has no analytics in it.
    </p>

    <h2>What the app stores on a server</h2>
    <p>Two things, and only these two.</p>
    <p>
      <strong>Notifications.</strong> If you allow notifications, the app sends the
      notification token that Apple issues for your device, the language you picked in
      the app, and whether the build is a test build or a released one. That token
      identifies a device to Apple's notification service, not a person. Turning
      notifications off in iOS stops the notifications; the stored token becomes unusable
      and is removed when Apple reports it as no longer valid.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Likes.</strong> Tapping the heart on an article sends the article and a
      random identifier that your device generates by itself and keeps locally. It is not
      derived from your device, your account or anything about you, and it exists so that
      the same article is not counted twice. The website does the same thing with a value
      in your browser's local storage.
    </p>

    <h2>What the app keeps on your device</h2>
    <p>
      Your language and theme, which articles you liked, and a copy of the news so the
      app opens without a connection. Deleting the app removes all of it.
    </p>

    <h2>The talent and Legacy calculators</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing you build is sent anywhere. A build lives in the link, which is why sharing
      one is copy and paste. Opening a shared link reads the build from the address and
      stores nothing.
    </p>

    <h2>The website</h2>
    <p>
      The website uses Google Analytics to count visits. The likes work as described
      above. The site is served as static files by GitHub Pages, which, like any web
      server, logs requests.
    </p>

    <h2>Videos and posts from other sites</h2>
    <p>
      A few news articles carry a YouTube video, a Reddit post or a post from X inside
      the page. Those frames load by themselves while you read the article, so YouTube,
      Reddit or X sees your IP address and can set their own cookies, even if you never
      press play. Nothing about you is passed to them by us. The YouTube frames use
      youtube-nocookie.com, the frames from X carry Do Not Track, and only the article you
      are reading loads such a frame.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Clips and Streams pages work the other way round: nothing is requested from
      YouTube or Twitch there until you click a clip.
    </p>

    <h2>Item tooltips on the BiS lists</h2>
    <p>
      Point at an item on a BiS list and the tooltip you see comes from Wowhead. It is
      drawn by a script of theirs that loads on those pages only, and only on a device
      with a real mouse, so on a phone or a tablet nothing is requested from Wowhead at
      all. Where it does load, Wowhead sees your IP address. The icons beside the item
      names are served by this site, so those cost you nothing with anyone else.
    </p>

    <h2>Other companies involved</h2>
    <p>
      Notifications go through Apple. Likes and notification tokens are stored with
      Supabase. Visit counts go to Google Analytics. The site is hosted by GitHub Pages.
      YouTube, Reddit, X and Twitch are involved only where their frames appear, as
      described above.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      The app is not aimed at children and collects nothing that identifies anyone, of any
      age.
    </p>

    <h2>Getting in touch</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this page, or about what the app stores, can go to
      contact@wowforever.be.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If what the app stores ever changes, this page changes with it. Last updated on
